  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{ABC}$ be a triangle of area $15 \\sqrt{2}$ and the vectors $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{AB}}=\\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-7 \\hat{k}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{BC}}=\\mathrm{a} \\hat{i}+\\mathrm{b} \\hat{j}+\\mathrm{ck}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{AC}}=6 \\hat{i}+\\mathrm{d} \\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k}, \\mathrm{~d}>0$. Then the square of the length of the largest side of the triangle $\\mathrm{ABC}$ is _______"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "54",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0051_d6a9b50f99b9.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Area }=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\\n1 & 2 & -7 \\\\\n6 & d & -2\n\\end{array}\\right|=15 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n& (-4+7 d) \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}(-2+42)+\\hat{k}(d-12) \\\\\n& (7 d-4)^2+(40)^2+(d-12)^2=1800 \\\\\n& 50 d^2-80 d-40=0 \\\\\n& 5 d^2-8 d-4=0 \\\\\n& 5 d^2-10 d-2 d-4 \\\\\n& 5 d(d-2)+2(d-2)=0 \\\\\n& d=2 \\text { or } d=-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\\n& \\because d>0, d=2 \\\\\n& (a+1) \\hat{i}+(b+2) \\hat{j}+(c-7) \\hat{k}=6 \\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k} \\\\\n& a+1=6 \\& b+2=2, c-7=-2 \\\\\n& a=5 \\quad b=0 \\quad c=5 \\\\\n& |A B|=\\sqrt{1+4+49}=\\sqrt{54} \\\\\n& |B C|=\\sqrt{25+25}=\\sqrt{50} \\\\\n& |A C|=\\sqrt{86+4+4}=\\sqrt{44}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Ans. 54"
  }
}